<title>JAPAN: Nomura shares ask-only after prosecutors' raid.</title>
<headline>Nomura shares ask-only after prosecutors' raid.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nomura Securities Co Ltd were ask-only in early Wednesday trade, after Japanese prosecutors raided the country's biggest brokerage late on Tuesday due to alleged illegal payments to &quot;sokaiya&quot;, or racketeers.</p>
<p>As of 0017 GMT, the share price was ask-only at 1,390 yen, against Tuesday's close of 1,440 yen.</p>
</text>
